===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|enm|frain|fraine|frainen|frayn|frayne|freinen|freyne}}
* {{alter|enm|fræine|fræinien|vraini||early}}
* {{alter|enm|fraȝȝnenn||Ormulum}}

===Etymology===
{{dercat|enm|ine-pro}}
{{inh+|enm|ang|fræġnian}}, variant of {{m|ang|freġnan}}, {{m|ang|friġnan||to inquire, ask}}, from {{inh|enm|gmw-pro|*fregnan}}, from {{inh|enm|gem-pro|*frehnaną}}; reinforced by {{cog|non|fregna}}.

{{rel-top|Cognates:}}
Cognate with {{cog|dum|vraghen|vrāghen|to ask}}, {{cog|gmh|vrāgen||to ask}}, Old {{cog|da|fregne||to ask}}, {{cog|lt|prašyti||to ask}}, Polish {{m|pl|prosić||to ask}}. {{rel-bottom}}

===Verb===
{{enm-verb|stem=frayn}}

# To [[ask]] or [[inquire]]; to make an [[inquiry]]:
## To [[ask]] or [[make]] a request {{gloss|for [[something]]}}.
##* '''fifteenth century''', unknown author, ''The prophecies of Thomas the Rhymer'':
##*: I '''frained''' fast what was his name, Where that he came, from what country.
## To [[ask]] or direct a [[question]] at [[someone]]:
##* {{quote-text|enm|year=c. 1370-90|author={{w|William Langland}}|title=Piers Plowman|section=I
|passage=Þanne I '''frained''' hir faire · for hym þat hir made. ''or'' Then I '''frayned''' at Faith what all that fare meant and who should joust in Jerusalem.}}
##* {{quote-text|enm|year=c. 1390|author=Geoffrey Chaucer|title=The Canterbury Tales
|passage=She '''fraineth''' and she prayeth pitously To every Jew that dwelt in thilke place To tell her if her child went ought forby.}}
##* {{RQ:Wakefield_Mystery_Plays|X|91|[Joseph:] Bot certys, mary, I rew full sore / It standys so with the[e] now. / Bot of a thyng '''frayn''' the[e] I shall / who owe this child thou gose with all? / ''Maria''. Syr, ye, and god of heuen.|Joseph: But Mary, I very much regret that circumstances are as they are with you. But one thing I will ask you: Who's child is this that you are pregnant with? / Mary: You, sir, and God of heaven.|lines=183–187}}
## To [[ask]] or [[put]] [[forward]] (a [[question]]).
# To [[look]] or [[search]] for something.
# To [[acquire]] [[knowledge]] through [[asking]].

